    text: ' The home page is the screen you come back to. It follows the framework you selected and shows, for that framework, how many in-scope controls have evidence and how many events are mapped. A Clauses card appears when the framework has clauses. The tasks offered follow your permissions.  The assurance workspace: evidence coverage for the chosen framework, what needs attention, and the tasks people start from.  Needs attention gathers the things worth a look: controls without evidence, open audits past their end date, and effectiveness measures whose latest numeric entry is outside its threshold. Choose Refresh to update the overview.  Explore your workspace keeps a connected view. Zoom into a framework section or a record, follow its evidence and relationships, then use Zoom out to retrace your path or Home to return to the overview.  A coverage count is a starting point, not a verdict. It tells you that linked evidence exists. Whether that evidence is relevant and sufficient is your judgement during review.  Going deeper: what Needs attention checks Threshold comparisons happen only when the measure and its entry use the same unit. Administrators also see enabled API collectors with consecutive failures; those collection checks cover the whole installation, whichever framework is selected. ',
