    text: ' An ingester can also feed an effectiveness measure. In the builder, expand Collect effectiveness measurements and select Evidence and a measured value . Choose an existing measure, use its exact unit, and map value , period_start and period_end (as YYYY-MM-DD) alongside the usual evidence fields.  KEEN compares each reported value with the measure’s threshold, and every observation links back to its source event with the collector’s revision and run. Before relying on the automation, inspect the measure’s observations and a passing and a failing example.  Going deeper: values, units and repeat periods The value must be finite and the period ordered correctly. Supply values in the measure’s unit and calculate aggregate percentages before submitting them, or use KEEN’s own calculation workflow. Reuse a stable observation ID when you collect the same reporting period again. ',
