    title: 'Set up a source connection',
    book: 'Using KEEN',
    url: 'using-collection.html#named-source-connections',
    text: ' Three words recur in the Sources screen. A source type is an adapter, such as Loki, GitLab or Forgejo. A connection is one endpoint or account with its credentials. Inputs choose what to collect through that connection: queries, projects, users or feed URLs.  Open Sources & Evidence Mapping → Sources and choose Define a source . Only source types enabled in the deployment are offered. Enter a name, endpoint and credentials, and save. Choose Add input to pick a user, organisation, repository, query or other supported input. Choose Add mapping rule on the input to connect its evidence to controls.  Use Edit source to change an address or credentials. Events show which connection captured them, and deleting a connection keeps its collected evidence and recorded identity.  Going deeper: rules that span connections When you create a mapping rule, choose either all connections of the source type or one named connection, then the inputs. All connections includes connections added later. ',
