    url: 'using-mapping.html#mapping-from-an-event',
    text: ' The quickest way to a good rule starts from the event page. Everything the rule needs is already on the screen.  Open an event and choose Create mapping from this event . Review the suggested conditions. Field names follow the event JSON, including structured keys such as fields → process.name , fields → host.name , fields → status and fields → log.file.path . Remove conditions that are too specific. A host or IP condition restricts the rule to that host or address, and event identifiers and timestamps identify single records rather than reusable evidence. Give the mapping a meaningful name and choose the framework controls or clauses. The suggestion button uses the name to find relevant controls; refine the name and try again if the suggestions miss. Review and save. The existing-mapping browser lets you search, edit or delete rules, and the historical-application action maps evidence already collected.  A mapping attributes matching evidence to framework requirements. Collection inputs decide which remote data KEEN fetches; a rule on its own does not configure a remote collection. ',
