    text: ' Questions can be attached to an evidence event, a risk, a PESTLE(E) item, a SWOT item or a story. They keep a reviewer’s uncertainty next to the material being reviewed.  A question thread on an event: who asked, when, its answered state and the reply box for the author or an administrator.  Open the record and its Questions area. Your account needs access to the record and permission to create questions. Write a specific question, such as “Which restore test does this result refer to, and where is its completion record?” For evidence questions, attach supporting files where useful. Other question types are text-only. Follow the questions you opened, and unread administrator replies, in My Questions . Administrators work from the Questions queue, filtered by unanswered, reviewing, answered or all threads. Return to the record to read the discussion in context. Administrators and the thread’s author can reply, subject to access checks.  Status Meaning Unanswered A new thread, or one reopened by a reply from its author. Reviewing An administrator is investigating. Answered An administrator has replied. Administrators can also set statuses explicitly.  A status records where the workflow stands. Whether the evidence is sufficient is still your assessment of the reply and its supporting material.  Going deeper: notifications and deletion Unread indicators help authors find responses. Optional administrator-configured question webhooks can notify Slack, Teams, Google Chat or a generic destination; the discussion itself stays in KEEN, and a reply in an external chat does not create a KEEN answer. Deleting a thread needs the question-delete permission and removes the discussion history, so prefer a reply or a status change when the review should be kept. ',
