    text: ' Evidence does not stay forever unless something protects it. Here is how retention and audit samples interact.  An administrator can retain evidence by maximum age or by maximum event count, or leave automatic retention off. Evidence sampled into an audit is protected while that audit exists. Removing the sample from the audit does not release the hold; deleting the audit does. Evidence also protected by another audit stays protected.  Going deeper: counts, purges and storage cleanup A maximum event count applies to unprotected events, so audit-protected evidence can make the total larger. A purge removes eligible evidence and schedules storage cleanup; object-lock or retention rules in the storage provider may delay physical deletion, and administrators can inspect pending cleanup. ',
