    title: 'Maintain the ISMS',
    book: 'Using KEEN',
    url: 'using-isms.html#11-maintain-the-isms',
    text: ' Objectives Intended outcomes, linked to controls, owners and effectiveness measures. Effectiveness measures and metrics A measure says how effectiveness is assessed; a metric is one dated observation or score for it. Documents Policies and processes, with folders, types, tags, rich text, version history and comments. Assets The resources you manage, with ownership, organisation relationships and related risks. Organisation chart Roles and reporting relationships. Roles can own risks. Access Matrix Who, or which role, should have access to an asset and at what level. It records intended access; grants and revocations happen in the external system. Application Configuration Relevant application settings, documented. Minutes of Meetings Decisions, discussion and attendance, including people without KEEN accounts.  Effectiveness measures: the latest value against its target, who owns the measure, the control it informs and the metric history behind it.  Before you add a metric, review the measure’s method, target and source. Some metrics arrive through configured webhooks. Where a measure records automatic zero values, read them as part of its method and check source coverage separately.  Save substantive document changes as a new content version, so the history shows which wording was in force at any time. If someone else edits at the same time, a reload reconciles their changes.  Going deeper: how ISMS links become evidence Linking an ISMS record to framework controls or clauses records an automatic Diary entry for the record. The entry lists its current control and clause references and counts towards the linked controls’ evidence. Revising the links updates the entry and credits each added mapping to the person who saved the record.  People and vendors  People & vendors holds personnel and supplier assurance. A person does not need a KEEN account: record their optional account, organisation role and assets, then add assurance records such as training, screening or policy acknowledgement. Each record can carry a category, requirement, status, completion and expiry dates, an authoritative source and an evidence link.  A vendor record holds supplier details and the assets it supplies. An asset has one supplying vendor, so assigning it to another vendor moves that relationship; review the effect before saving. ',
