    text: ' The Asset Matrix and the assets used by risk assessments are the same records. Create an asset once and select it in risks, supplier records and personnel relationships. An asset can be a device, an information set, a service or an agreed group; say which in its description.  The asset matrix: category, subcategory, licence, owner, register holder and linked CIA risks for each asset.  Keep the organisation chart current first: an asset’s owner and register custodian are links to its nodes. In ISMS → Asset Matrix , create or edit the asset’s name and description, choose a category and a subcategory that belongs to it, and a licence where applicable. Set Owner (who is responsible for the asset) and Register held by (who maintains its inventory information). Link controls and clauses in the selected framework, save, and check the links and changelog on the detail page. In People and Vendors, associate the asset with its people and supplier. In Risks, select the existing asset for the assessments that concern it. When the asset changes, review its risks, users, supplier and controls together. A name change never needs a duplicate asset.  Example. Create “Staff laptops” with a description of which devices it covers, an IT ownership node and a register custodian. Link the endpoint controls, the supplier and the people, and use the asset in a loss or theft risk. In an audit, sample the asset together with real endpoint evidence; the register entry alone only shows what was recorded. ',
