    text: ' A reporting job in another system can post observations straight into a measure. KEEN writes the example call for you.  In ISMS → Effectiveness measures , define the measure with its metric key, unit and thresholds, and save it. Expand Send measurements from another system in the editor or on the measure’s detail page, and copy the generated curl or Python example into your reporting job. It already contains this installation’s endpoint, the metric key, the framework and the unit. Replace the example value of zero with the observed result. Optional period_start and period_end describe the reporting period as YYYY-MM-DD . Supply the webhook secret your administrator configured as KEEN_METRICS_SECRET in the reporting environment, and KEEN_METRICS_HEADER if a custom header is configured. The examples reference these as environment variables.  Each successful POST creates a metric entry, so repeated submissions produce additional entries. KEEN evaluates each result against the measure’s threshold. Review it, link it to the relevant requirements and sample supporting evidence into an audit when appropriate.  Going deeper: the webhook behind the examples Your administrator configures the isms_metrics webhook and its secret in the deployment. Measurements are evidence of observed performance, such as service availability or patch coverage; the threshold remains the criterion KEEN applies. ',
