    title: 'Plan audits and sample evidence',
    book: 'Using KEEN',
    url: 'using-audits.html#audits-and-sampling',
    text: ' An audit in KEEN is a container for one review: its scope, the people involved, the evidence you examined, your findings and the report. This chapter walks one audit from start to completion, then covers scheduled audits and the coverage views that tell you what has not been looked at lately.  Scope The controls, clauses and documents the audit sets out to examine. A statement of intent. Sample A record you actually examined: an event, a risk, a document, a measure and so on. Finding The result of your assessment of a requirement against the samples.  audits.manage lets you create audits and scheduled templates and run or edit the ones you created. audits.admin also edits other people’s audits and deletes audits or templates. Sampling evidence also needs read access to the underlying event or record, for administrators too.  Scope Coverage: how many controls, clauses and documents audits have included so far, and a gap matrix of what still needs coverage. ',
