    text: ' Open Audits → Scheduled Audits . Enter the title, audit type and planning notes; the schedule belongs to the framework selected in the top navigation. Choose the date rule and its first run date, or the first-weekday month and year fields the rule offers. Check the date against the working days of that month. Set the end date or duration, the recurrence, the interval and an Until date where appropriate. Select the policies and processes in scope, add attendees with name, account, e-mail and role, and save. Check the template’s calendar placement. Before the date, confirm the audit record was created; creation happens within the configured lead time ( KEEN_SCHEDULED_AUDIT_CREATE_DAYS_AHEAD ). Open the created audit and review its scope and participants. A later template change does not rewrite an existing occurrence.  If an occurrence is missing, ask the administrator to check the scheduling logs and look-ahead window before creating a manual audit, so you avoid duplicates.  In Scope Coverage , choose the audit source, date range and filters to see which controls, clauses and documents have been included in audits, and follow the links back to those audits. Use the gaps to plan coverage, then judge sample sufficiency and findings for each requirement. ',
