    text: ' Celery beat enqueues scheduled work and the workers execute it. When a collection, an audit occurrence or a historical mapping job is missing, look at both sides: is beat running (one instance only), and is a worker consuming its queue? Audit creation also waits for the configured look-ahead window, so a template can exist before its first audit does.  For effectiveness metrics, send one authenticated payload and confirm it appears under the intended measure with the right key, value, unit, period and source. When a trend looks odd, distinguish repeated delivery, missing observations and automatically recorded zeros. Mail, calendar invitations and question or incident webhooks each need their own outbound configuration. Diagnose delivery failures without repeatedly notifying recipients, and keep the application record and the upstream acknowledgement as separate evidence. ',
