    url: 'using-operations.html#notification-configuration',
    text: ' Question discussions work inside KEEN on their own. For notifications, administrators can set KEEN_QUESTION_WEBHOOK_SLACK_URLS , KEEN_QUESTION_WEBHOOK_TEAMS_URLS , KEEN_QUESTION_WEBHOOK_GOOGLE_CHAT_URLS and KEEN_QUESTION_WEBHOOK_GENERIC_URLS ; generic headers and webhook signing have their own settings. Test with a clearly labelled test question.  Incident declaration needs KEEN_INCIDENT_WEBHOOK_URL , with optional headers, signing secret, signature-header name and timeout in the matching KEEN_INCIDENT_WEBHOOK_* settings. KEEN saves a declaration after a successful HTTP response; the receiving service owns the ticket from there.  Grant question.create , question.delete , incident.create and incident.delete according to responsibilities. Reading a record does not grant every action on it; replies are for the thread author and administrators, and the central question queue is administrative. ',
