    text: ' In Evidence retention, choose Add override and select Source type or Rule ID . Changing the scope clears the selection. Pick an existing value from the dropdown; labels and rule descriptions appear beside their exact identifiers. Source types use the event’s source value, such as github or keen-agent , and cover every connection of that type. Choose Keep everything, Maximum age (days) or Newest events to keep. Preview shows the combined effect of the global policy and all proposed overrides; Save applies it to existing and future evidence.  Rule overrides take priority over source-type overrides, which take priority over the global policy. Remove an override row to restore inheritance. The source detail page and the mapping rule editor each link to their retention settings, and overrides whose source or rule no longer exists stay labelled Unavailable — saved override for review or removal.  Going deeper: how rule overrides and counts are evaluated A rule override applies to events with recorded automatic mappings from that rule, across frameworks; it does not re-run the rule’s current conditions. If several overridden rules own an event, every applicable rule policy must permit deletion, and Keep everything on any of them preserves the event. Disabling or deleting a rule does not remove its retention override, because existing recorded mappings still determine ownership; removing or remapping those links can change which policy applies, and a deleted rule’s override can be removed in Evidence retention. Count limits apply separately to each policy group. The global count covers events with no applicable override; a source count covers events of that type with no applicable rule override; a rule count covers its automatically mapped events, counting each event once even when it maps to several controls. An event shared by several overridden rules counts in each rule’s allowance, and audit-held events remain additional to every allowance. To stop all automatic deletion, set the global policy and every override to Keep everything, or remove the overrides. ',
