    text: ' Symptom Check API fails at startup Its logs for invalid settings, database connectivity and migration errors; that the configured database exists and the credentials match. Worker or beat cannot connect KEEN_REDIS_URL and the private service network. UI loads but requests fail The browser-visible error and the nginx and API logs. Browser API URLs begin /api/v1/ ; the API receives /v1/ . Check proxy rewrites, TLS forwarding and cookie settings. A 401 concerns authentication; a 403 can concern permission or CSRF. Never resolve either by disabling the control. OIDC fails The exact issuer, client, callback URL, JWKS and host origin; clock accuracy; whether a prior login state was already consumed. In hosted mode, confirm the correct owner subject without exposing ID tokens or client secrets in logs. Ingestion is disabled The adapter flag. Ingestion runs without evidence Its collection items, credentials, upstream permissions, filters and cursor. Evidence arrives but does not map Preview the definition against that exact event; check collector identity, field values and existing framework targets. S3 AccessDenied The runtime principal, bucket, prefix, encryption key and any required conditional-write headers. In hosted mode a denial against another customer’s resource is expected. Never add wildcard permissions. Stale UI behaviour or counts The deployed UI image and asset cache before changing data; the aggregation and cache refresh path for counts. Failed mail or outgoing webhooks The task result and destination configuration; avoid repeated notifications while diagnosing. ',
