    text: ' Frameworks, their nodes and the mapping rules that attach evidence to them are rows in PostgreSQL, edited through the application. This chapter covers the framework editor, evidence definitions and the shared condition evaluator.  api/routes/frameworks.py exposes framework listing and upsert and the administrator node editor; the UI controller is pages/framework-editor.js embedded in admin.html. It manages framework metadata and Clause, Control and Custom nodes with descriptions, upstream URLs, ordering, scope and parent relationships.  Two representations of a clause. ControlItem identities include framework, kind and reference, and clause nodes also maintain first-class FrameworkClause records used by clause views and ControlClauseLink relationships. Keep both consistent when modifying the editor, and keep slugs and node kind/reference stable.  Going deeper: deletion, seed data and provenance Parents must belong to the appropriate framework or category and form a valid hierarchy. Deletion checks children, clause links and mappings before allowing removal; extend dependency handling deliberately when adding another relationship type. The release migrations 0001_release_schema.py and 0002_release_seed.py define the schema and seed the bundled catalogues. The frozen OSA snapshot supplies 88 of the 94 frameworks; KEEN Assurance, DVSTF, Cyber Essentials and Risk Ledger supply four more, alongside the two ISO 9001 editions. Bundled JSON provides deterministic migration input, everyday catalogue edits use database records through the web editor, and seed logic must preserve administrator edits. Upstream publication links identify authoritative text and its usage rights. ',
