    text: ' Risks, documents, people, assets and SWOT items are ordinary application records with their own services, access rules and version checks. This chapter names the module that owns each one.  api/routes/risks.py handles scenarios and control links; api/routes/risk_register.py adds register views, ratings, thresholds, CSV exchange and reusable templates. Risk is the shared scenario entity: the editor, register and heatmap use the same inherent and residual likelihood and impact fields, each constrained to 1–5, with scores calculated as their product.  RiskLibraryEntry stores reusable scenario text, CIA associations, treatment guidance and suggested assessment data. Creating from a template produces a reviewable risk, and later template changes do not rewrite that assessment. Risk creation receives library_template_id ; the server retrieves suggested KEEN-AF control references from the stored template, filters them against remaining controls and writes those links under KEEN-AF:1.0, even when the active framework is different.  Going deeper: migrations and CSV exchange The release schema and seed migrations supply the risk library, unified risk and asset records, and template control mappings; earlier incremental migrations are archived in alembic/legacy_versions/ . Use the active release migration chain when inspecting or extending a fresh installation. CSV import creates new scenarios and validates the complete file before committing, with size and row limits and validation of ownership, ratings and control references. Export protects spreadsheet cells against formula interpretation. Preserve whole-file rejection and formula-safe output when changing the schema. ',
